  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S. S.A. Sugandh Pvt. Ltd vs The Chairman on 24 April, 2024 Author: S.K. Panigrahi Bench: S.K. Panigrahi IN THE HIGH COURT OF ORISSA AT CUTTACK W.P.(C) No.34274 of 2023 M/s. S.A. Sugandh Pvt. Ltd., .... Petitioner Chhatisgarh Represented By Sr. Adv. Mr. S. P. Mishra Along with Mr. V. Mohapatra -versus- The Chairman, State Pollution .... Opposite Parties Control Board, Bhubaneswar & Ors. Represented By Adv. Mr. S. P. Mohanty Mr. P. K. Parhi, DSGI Mr. I. Mohanty, ASC CORAM: DR. JUSTICE S.K. PANIGRAHI ORDER Order 24.04.2024 No. 05. 1. This matter is taken up through hybrid arrangement. 2 . T h e P e t i t i o n e r , i n t h i s W r i t P e t i t i o n , c h a l l e n g e s t h e c o m m u n i c a t i o n No.2334/IIICON(NOC/02/2022-23) dated 06.07.2023 issued by the Regional Officer, State Pollution Control Board/Opposite Party No.5 under Annexure-4 // 2 // rejecting its application for grant of CTE manufacture of Tobacco and Tobacco Products of 2400 TPA from Raw Tobacco, Perfume, Kiwam of 2400 TPA at Sandasingha, PO-Sasan, Dist-Sambalpur. M/S. S.A. Sugandh Pvt. Ltd vs The Chairman on 24 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/163608439/ 1 4.",
    "facts": "The State Pollution Control Board specifically does not attribute any reason for the unit which is polluting in any form. Accordingly, the impugned order dated 06.07.2023 was issued to the present Petitioner refusing to grant consent to establish for manufacture of Tobacco and Tobacco products of 2400 TPA from Raw Tobacco, perfume, Kiwam of 2400 TPA under Annexure-4. 6. In the said letter, the State Pollution Control Board, Odisha has stated that the Health and Family Welfare Department has prohibited the manufacture, storage, sale and distribution of Gutkha and Panmasala containing Tobacco/nicotine as the ingredients by whatsoever name available in the market. 7. Considering the letter dated 16.03.2024 issued by the Health and Family Welfare Department, Government of Odisha wherein, it has been clearly stated that the Chewing Tobacco is not a prohibited item under Section 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, the communication No.2334/IIICON(NOC/02/2022-23) dated 06.07.2023 issued by the Regional Officer, State Pollution // 4 // Control Board/Opposite Party No.5 and the communication No.14493/IND-IV-BW-3436 dated 13.09.2023 issued by the Chief Environmental Engineer, Bhubaneswar/Opposite Party No.4 are [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "arguments": "At the outset, learned counsel for the State brings to the notice of this Court to the letter dated 16.03.2024 issued by the Health and Family Welfare Department, Government of Odisha wherein, it has been stated that the product Chewing Tobacco is excluded from the category of the goods prohibited products under the notification No.367 dated 03.01.2013 issued under Section 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 5."
  },
